Free-radical chlorination of racemic 2-chlorobutane gives four structural dichlorobutanes:
1. 1,2-Dichlorobutane: $1$ chiral centre $\implies 2$ optically active enantiomers;
2. 2,2-Dichlorobutane: achiral ($0$ optically active isomers);
3. 2,3-Dichlorobutane: $2$ identical chiral centres $\implies 1$ optically inactive *meso* isomer $+ 2$ optically active enantiomers;
4. 1,3-Dichlorobutane: $1$ chiral centre $\implies 2$ optically active enantiomers.
Total optically active isomers $= 2 + 0 + 2 + 2 = 6$.

